**Yariakam (یاریەکەم)** is a gaming commerce project conceived as a destination for purchasing digital games and gift cards across platforms including Xbox, PlayStation, PC, and mobile.

The project is **in development**. This case study documents the product direction and engineering decisions being explored, not a completed production marketplace.

## Product Requirements

Digital gaming products have a different purchasing experience from ordinary physical goods. The platform needs a clear way to present products, platforms, regional variations, and purchase-related information so customers can understand what they are selecting.

Early work has focused on defining the storefront experience and the relationship between the customer-facing catalog and the management tools that support it.

## Architecture Direction

**ASP.NET Core** was selected for backend development, reflecting the requirement for a maintainable service layer and a structured foundation for future commerce workflows.

The frontend direction distinguishes the public storefront from internal management interfaces. The public experience prioritizes the identity and usability of a gaming marketplace, while administrative tooling can rely on more conventional reusable application components.

<Callout title="Development Status">
  Yariakam is an active product-development initiative. Payment processing, fulfillment, launch readiness, and other production capabilities are not represented here as completed work.
</Callout>

## Engineering Focus

The project provides an opportunity to work through system design decisions before they become expensive to change. This includes defining feature boundaries, considering reusable UI patterns, and selecting technologies appropriate for an evolving commerce product.

As development progresses, the case study can be expanded with real screenshots, implemented workflows, and verified outcomes.

